WEBVTT

00:00:00,880 --> 00:00:14,200
How long do you have to wait to take supplements before your blood work or

00:00:14,200 --> 00:00:18,960
doesn't not matter? It doesn't really matter at all. So your supplements shouldn't

00:00:18,960 --> 00:00:29,160
affect your blood work really at all. So when you're getting just a CBC or a

00:00:29,160 --> 00:00:35,260
complete metabolic panel or you're getting full testing for food

00:00:35,260 --> 00:00:40,020
sensitivities or anything, your supplements taking your supplements right before

00:00:40,020 --> 00:00:44,100
you do your blood work. It literally has no effect on your blood work. I've

00:00:44,100 --> 00:00:47,380
not seen anything about supplements that affect your blood work. So you don't

00:00:47,380 --> 00:00:50,980
have to worry about that. The only thing I will say about blood work is that it's

00:00:50,980 --> 00:00:57,100
always best to do it 12 hour fast. So I know sometimes that's just not

00:00:57,100 --> 00:01:01,940
convenient. You're going in to get a blood test at four o'clock in the afternoon.

00:01:01,940 --> 00:01:08,260
You would have fasted all day. A lot of the blood markers are fast. It really

00:01:08,260 --> 00:01:14,660
makes no difference. It does make a difference on your glucose levels and some

00:01:14,660 --> 00:01:20,980
other factors, some other markers as well. Definitely your glucose levels. Now

00:01:20,980 --> 00:01:27,180
with the advent of home cominers and people that have a whole glucometer, you

00:01:27,180 --> 00:01:34,340
know, your glucose level on your blood test on a CBC makes a little, you're

00:01:34,340 --> 00:01:39,140
not really looking at that. Then if you're able to measure your own glucose levels

00:01:39,140 --> 00:01:48,020
throughout the day and post eating and so it's not as make a deal. But typically it's

00:01:48,020 --> 00:01:55,500
always better to do a 12 hour fast before you're doing any blood work. So you'd

00:01:55,500 --> 00:01:59,700
want a schedule in a perfect case scenario schedule your blood work to go

00:01:59,700 --> 00:02:02,580
in at nine o'clock or eight o'clock in the morning to get your blood work and you

00:02:02,580 --> 00:02:07,820
haven't eaten since eight o'clock at night before. That's going to be your best

00:02:07,820 --> 00:02:12,260
thing. That's going to be your best picture to get your blood work. The other good

00:02:12,260 --> 00:02:16,660
thing to look at when you get blood work done is that you do it at the same time

00:02:16,660 --> 00:02:21,420
each time you do it. So if you let's say you're getting blood work every month or

00:02:21,420 --> 00:02:25,300
every three months or every six months, you try to schedule it at nine o'clock in the

00:02:25,300 --> 00:02:30,300
morning every time you go to get your blood work done and you do a 12 hour fast

00:02:30,300 --> 00:02:34,580
on each one. You're going to get just more accurate comparisons.

